Does this compile with `tsc --strict`? If not, which statement fails, and why?

```ts
const a: any = "hello";
a.launch();
const u: unknown = "hello";
u.launch();
if (typeof u === "string") {
  console.log(u.toUpperCase());
}
```

**Fix lengthOf(value: unknown)**

This doesn't compile: `value` is `unknown`. Return the length of a string or array, and 0 for anything else — including objects that happen to have a `length` property.

```ts
function lengthOf(value: unknown): number {
  return value.length;
}
```

back:
// Why: Narrow unknown with real checks. Switching to any compiles, but then anything with
// a length gets through.
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/narrowing.html
function lengthOf(value: unknown): number {
  if (typeof value === "string" || Array.isArray(value)) return value.length;
  return 0;
}

